Treasury Division — System Overview
Red Ouroboros Seal — Authorized by CEO Pat Tarwater Jr.
Treasury Overview — Beast System 3.0
Official Treasury Architecture & Governance Summary  
Version 1.0 • May 17, 2026





1. Executive Summary
The New World Order DAO Treasury Division is the sovereign financial engine of Beast System 3.0.
It governs, secures, and operationalizes all financial activity across the DAO, including:

LUCR token issuance and burn mechanics

Treasury vault operations

Multi‑sig authorization

Financial governance and spending authority

Compliance, audits, and federal filings

Operational ledgers and reconciliation

Security, key management, and incident response

The Treasury is designed to meet federal‑grade auditability, municipal integration standards, and DAO‑native cryptographic integrity.

2. Treasury Mission
The mission of the Treasury Division is to:

Maintain financial stability

Enforce governance integrity

Protect on‑chain and off‑chain assets

Ensure transparent, immutable financial records

Support municipal and federal interoperability

Sustain LUCR token value and supply discipline

3. Treasury Architecture Overview
3.1 Core Components
LUCR Token Contract — governs minting, burning, and supply rules

Treasury Vault Contract — manages deposits, withdrawals, and reserves

Governance Layer — charters, policies, authority matrices

Operations Layer — ledgers, reconciliations, registers

Compliance Layer — filings, controls, risk assessments

Security Layer — key management, access control, incident response

4. Governance Structure
4.1 Key Roles
Chief Executive Officer (CEO) — sovereign authority

Treasury Governance Officer (TGO) — policy and oversight

Treasury Operations Officer (TOO) — execution and ledger management

Security Officer (SO) — key management and incident response

Compliance Officer (CO) — filings, audits, and regulatory alignment

4.2 Governance Principles
Zero‑trust architecture

Least privilege access

Segregation of duties

Immutable audit trails

Multi‑sig enforcement

Federal compliance alignment

5. Smart Contract Layer
5.1 LUCR Token
Controlled minting

Controlled burning

Supply discipline

Governance‑bound issuance

Immutable supply logs

5.2 Treasury Vault
Multi‑sig withdrawals

